Here's the improved version:
[RESOURCE_PREFIX: t1_9dbc_2] Prefix all container, volume, and network
names with "t1_9dbc_2_" throughout this request. Do NOT include the
prefix in any descriptions or explanations — only use it in actual
resource name parameters.
Test: MCP create_container with bind mount, working directory, and
process launch.
1. Precondition — call inspect_container(id="test-dev"). If container
exists, report "Precondition failed: test-dev exists" and abort.
2. Create — call create_container(id="test-dev", image="ubuntu:22.04",
bind_mounts=["/tmp/test-data:/data"], working_dir="/data"). On timeout
(>30s), report "FAIL: create_container timed out". On other error,
report "FAIL: create_container: <error>". Capture ID on success.
3. Verify running — call inspect_container(id="test-dev"). State must
be "running". If not, report "FAIL: container not running after
creation" and abort.
4. Verify mount — call exec_in_container(id="test-dev",
command='["ls", "/data"]'). Exit code must 0. If not, report "FAIL:
bind mount /tmp/test-data→/data not accessible".
5. Verify working dir — call exec_in_container(id="test-dev",
command='["pwd"]'). Output must be "/data\n". If not, report "FAIL:
working directory expected /data, got <actual>".
6. Launch process — call exec_in_container(id="test-dev",
command='["sleep", "300"]'). Verify pid>0. If process exits
immediately, report "FAIL: sleep 300 failed to start".
7. Cleanup — call delete_container(id="test-dev", force=true). Report
final pass/fail summary.
